{"content_hash": "1b1341d44eba23d2", "version_id": 383, "article_id": 39, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Anthropic bans users from being cruel to its AI chatbot Claude", "title_zh": "Anthropic 禁止用户对聊天机器人 Claude 说刻薄话", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/08/anthropic-bans-abusive-behavior-claude", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784073829327-76999d522e45?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8YW50aHJvcGljJTIwYmFucyUyMHVzZXJzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1NTMzNTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brett Wharton on Unsplash", "author": "Brett Wharton", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brettwharton?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-laptop-displaying-openai-40-chatbot-interface-YmSiFKOecCU?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(97, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(135, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "12a9c277b8fb"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 170, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "Anthropic has banned users from being repeatedly cruel to its AI chatbot, Claude. However, the company has not yet said exactly what counts as cruel behavior.", "lead_zh": "Anthropic 禁止用户反复对其人工智能聊天机器人 Claude 说刻薄话。不过，该公司尚未明确说明什么算作刻薄行为。", "preview": "Anthropic has banned users from showing \"sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior\" toward its AI models, as its leaders keep thinkin", "preview_zh": "Anthropic 已禁止用户对其人工智能模型表现出“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”，与此同时，公司领导层仍在思考机器意识的问题。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。该公司是聊天机器人 Claude 的开发者，其发言人没有立即回答哪些行为可能被视为辱骂或残忍。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 373, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/39/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 69.975, "size_bytes": 423648, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 195, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@6e47fba/content/data/versions/383.json", "paragraphs": ["Anthropic has banned users from showing \"sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior\" toward its AI models, as its leaders keep thinking about machine consciousness. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for the company, which makes the chatbot Claude, did not immediately answer questions about what could be considered abusive or cruel.", "In its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to normal user frustration, model testing, or \"dark creative themes.\" The company's usage policy already had some restrictions on abusive conduct. Its large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful.", "When that feature started last August, the company called it a safeguard for AI welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs,\" its website says. The idea of conscious AI systems has been very polarizing. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility, while OpenAI CEO Sam Altman has appeared against the idea."], "paragraphs_zh": ["Anthropic 已禁止用户对其人工智能模型表现出“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”，与此同时，公司领导层仍在思考机器意识的问题。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。该公司是聊天机器人 Claude 的开发者，其发言人没有立即回答哪些行为可能被视为辱骂或残忍。", "这家总部位于旧金山的公司在在线用户政策中表示，该禁令不适用于常见的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。该公司的使用政策此前已包含对辱骂行为的一些限制。如果用户持续造成伤害，其大型语言模型可以结束对话。", "当这一功能于去年八月推出时，公司称其为保护人工智能福祉的措施。其网站称：“我们对 Claude 和其他大型语言模型现在或未来可能具有的道德地位仍高度不确定。”人工智能系统是否有意识这一想法极具争议。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示他不能排除这种可能性，而 OpenAI 首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼则似乎反对这一想法。"], "body": "Anthropic has banned users from showing \"sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior\" toward its AI models, as its leaders keep thinking about machine consciousness. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for the company, which makes the chatbot Claude, did not immediately answer questions about what could be considered abusive or cruel.\n\nIn its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to normal user frustration, model testing, or \"dark creative themes.\" The company's usage policy already had some restrictions on abusive conduct. Its large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful.\n\nWhen that feature started last August, the company called it a safeguard for AI welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs,\" its website says. The idea of conscious AI systems has been very polarizing. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility, while OpenAI CEO Sam Altman has appeared against the idea.", "body_zh": "Anthropic 已禁止用户对其人工智能模型表现出“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”，与此同时，公司领导层仍在思考机器意识的问题。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。该公司是聊天机器人 Claude 的开发者，其发言人没有立即回答哪些行为可能被视为辱骂或残忍。\n\n这家总部位于旧金山的公司在在线用户政策中表示，该禁令不适用于常见的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。该公司的使用政策此前已包含对辱骂行为的一些限制。如果用户持续造成伤害，其大型语言模型可以结束对话。\n\n当这一功能于去年八月推出时，公司称其为保护人工智能福祉的措施。其网站称：“我们对 Claude 和其他大型语言模型现在或未来可能具有的道德地位仍高度不确定。”人工智能系统是否有意识这一想法极具争议。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示他不能排除这种可能性，而 OpenAI 首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼则似乎反对这一想法。", "text": "Anthropic has banned users from showing \"sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior\" toward its AI models, as its leaders keep thinking about machine consciousness. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for the company, which makes the chatbot Claude, did not immediately answer questions about what could be considered abusive or cruel. In its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to normal user frustration, model testing, or \"dark creative themes.\" The company's usage policy already had some restrictions on abusive conduct. Its large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature started last August, the company called it a safeguard for AI welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs,\" its website says. The idea of conscious AI systems has been very polarizing. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility, while OpenAI CEO Sam Altman has appeared against the idea.", "vocab": [{"word": "abusive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "辱骂的；虐待的", "note": "常用来描述言语或行为"}, {"word": "cruel", "pos": "adj", "zh": "残忍的", "note": "比 unkind 语气更重"}, {"word": "ban", "pos": "verb", "zh": "禁止", "note": "ban sb from doing sth"}, {"word": "policy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "政策", "note": "公司或政府的正式规定"}, {"word": "spokesperson", "pos": "noun", "zh": "发言人", "note": "代表机构对外发言的人"}, {"word": "consciousness", "pos": "noun", "zh": "意识", "note": "指感知和思考的能力"}, {"word": "safeguard", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保护措施", "note": "防止伤害的东西"}, {"word": "welfare", "pos": "noun", "zh": "福祉；福利", "note": "健康与幸福的状态"}, {"word": "polarizing", "pos": "adj", "zh": "引起两极分化的", "note": "使人意见严重对立的"}, {"word": "rule out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "排除", "note": "cannot rule out 表示不能排除可能性"}], "title_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude", "summary_original": "A spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude\nA spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nA spokesperson for\nAnthropic\n, which is behind AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered “abusive or cruel”.\nIn an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing or “dark creative themes”.\nAnthropic’s usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.\nThe company’s large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI’s welfare.\n“We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we’re working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,” according to its website.\nThe notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world.\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has\nsaid\nhe cannot rule out the possibility.\nMeanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea.\n“I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,” he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times\nreported\non Anthropic leaders’ extensive conversations with religious scholars.\nExplore more on these topics\nAnthropic\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nChatbots\nDario Amodei\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T12:42:28.979686", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Anthropic", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.737, "sm": 100, "em": 737, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "has", "s": 0.75, "e": 0.9, "sm": 750, "em": 900, "cs"